  m_Name: PatPre1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "After a biopsy, your physician mentions there is a small amount of tissue
    left over that isn\u2019t needed for your care. She asks if you would like to
    discard it or donate the leftover sample to a biobank for research. \r\n\r\n<b>Patient
    samples, such as blood or tissue, can be used in preclinical research to investigate
    how a treatment might work.</b>\nIs this <b>true</b> or <b>false</b>?"
  explanation: Patient samples are a powerful tool. They help researchers see how
    a disease actually behaves in the body, identify promising targets for treatment,
    and even provide early clues about how people may respond to a new treatment.
    Without patient samples, researchers would be missing a crucial window into the
    real-world biology of disease.
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Patient
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: PreClinical
